{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The complement of a graph, as a lazy view. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"complementView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ComplementView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices and their indices are the base’s. Row "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"j ≠ i"},{"type":"text","text":" that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base’s row "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" lacks, ascending: the row iterator marks the base row in a mask of ⌈n\/64⌉ words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(deg + n\/64), then yields the clear bits. A row costs O(n\/64 + output) and one allocation."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The complement of a sparse graph has Θ(n²) edges, so a traversal is Θ(n²) whatever the layout."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is its cell of the adjacency matrix, "},{"code":"Cell(source: i, target: j)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", ordered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row-major as "},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s positions are; an undirected edge has "},{"code":"source < target","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". There"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are no edge indices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"maps (","type":"text"},{"code":"[map, of:]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"values(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Its edges are not the base’s, so no edge map reads through.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"ComplementView","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ComplementView","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ComplementView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView.swift#L44"},"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations14ComplementViewV","modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ComplementView","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/complementview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/Cell",